{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5c1e2a90-4b7d-4a1e-9f3c-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
    "name": "Marina1 — Slip Management (Steel Thread)",
    "description": "End-to-end walkthrough of the Storable slip-management API.\n\nRun the requests IN ORDER (use the Collection Runner, or send them top-to-bottom). Each request captures the ids it creates into collection variables, so the whole thread is self-chaining — no manual copying.\n\nThe story:\n1. Prove the system is up and healthy.\n2. Show there are NO marinas yet.\n3. Create a marina, then show it has NO slips.\n4. Create a slip, a person, and their boat.\n5. Prove the guardrails: an oversized boat is rejected, and a slip can't be double-booked.\n6. Lease the slip (a SlipHolding), and watch the slip flip to 'occupied'.\n7. Invoice the holding and take two payments (partial -> paid).\n8. Add a waitlist entry.\n9. End the holding and watch the slip free up again.\n\nPREREQUISITES:\n- Start the API:  .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe main.py   (listens on http://127.0.0.1:5000)\n- Start from a FRESH database so the 'empty' steps read true: delete storable.db before running.\n- baseUrl defaults to http://127.0.0.1:5000 — change the collection variable if yours differs.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "marina_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "slip_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "person_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "boat_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "oversized_boat_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "holding_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "invoice_id", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 · Health check (system is up)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('System reports healthy', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('healthy');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["health"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
